/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flowsheetDict  --  agitation01_helical_ribbon_polymer_melt

  A stirred vessel (`agitatedVessel`) holding the book's inelastic polymer melt (rho 980 kg/m3,
  power law m = 200 Pa s^n, n = 0.5), mixed by a helical ribbon with a tip speed of 1 m/s in a
  2.2 m tank.  WHO OWNS WHAT (R7): the flow curve is the FLUID's (the property dictionary,
  constant/experiments/powerLawEx85.dat); the Metzner-Otto constant k_s = 30 and the laminar
  power constant K_p (eq. 8.7, from the ribbon's geometry) are the IMPELLER's (the asset record
  constant/assets/helicalRibbonEx85.dat, kind impeller); the shear rate gamma_avg = k_s N is the
  UNIT's, and the unit asks the property door (form 3) for the apparent viscosity there.

  The shaft power is a Work item of the unit, W_shaft_kW, exactly as a pump's: it enters the plant
  boundary of the energy balance and leaves as the jacket's duty (isothermal, the default).

  ANCHOR.  The book prints (Example 8.5, p. 417-418): D = 2.095 m, N = 0.152 Hz (9.1 rpm),
  gamma_avg = 4.56 1/s, mu_avg = 93.7 Pa s, Re = 6.98, K_p = 494, P = 9838 W (9.84 kW), and the
  check Re_cr = 183/Po^(1/3) = 44 (laminar).  The book's own geometry has H/D = 1.5, past the
  1.30 of eq. 8.7's data (p. 386): the case runs it as a HYPOTHESIS and says so.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        M1;
        type        agitatedVessel;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( stirred );

        operation
        {
            vessel    { D_T 2.2 m; }
            impeller  { record helicalRibbonEx85; tipSpeed 1.0 m/s; }
            thermalMode isothermal;
            outsideCorrelationWindow
            {
                reason "the book's own Example 8.5 takes H/D = 1.5, past the 0.88-1.30 of the 148 configurations eq. 8.7 was fitted to (p. 386, 417); reproduced as printed";
            }
        }
    }
);
